<!-- Added by Plutext Pty Ltd for the docx4j FO renderer (docx4j-fo-renderer), a modified distribution derived
     from Apache FOP 2.12: a box beside a side float that would cross the page's foot goes to the next page
     (fop/CR-036). -->
<testcase>
  <info>
    <p>
      A line beside a side float that would cross the page's foot goes to the next page, as it does with no float.
      The body is 300pt tall, the float's foot within it, seven 9pt lines beside it with 6pt between. First sequence:
      the last line ends at 299pt and stays. Second: it would end at 303pt and opens the next page. Third: the same
      with no float. Fourth: the lines carry space-before, and the moved line's is discarded at the page's top, as at
      any page break. Fifth: the line would cross the foot straight after the float's start edge, where its list has
      no break before it, and it goes to the next page with nothing beside the float. Sixth and seventh: a line after
      a start edge that fits by 1pt below a space, its own space-before and the space-after above, stays beside the
      float. Eighth: a line after an end edge that fits by 1pt keeps its space-before and stays. Ninth: a line after a
      start edge that crosses the foot only by its block's border goes to the next page. Fop/CR-036 §6: the space at
      the edge was counted twice in the sixth to eighth.
    </p>
  </info>
  <fo>
